107396	107547	105281	105282	Little Billee	351	" Once I actually walked in my sleep -- and woke up in the market - place at Prague -- and found an immense crowd , and poor Svengali bleeding from the forehead , in a faint on the ground . He 'd been knocked down by a horse and cart , he told me . He 'd got his guitar with him . I suppose he and Gecko had been playing somewhere , for Gecko had his fiddle . If Gecko had n't been there , I do n't know what we should have done . You never saw such queer people as they were -- such crowds -- you'd think they 'd never seen an Englishwoman before . The noise they made , and the things they gave me ... some of them went down on their knees , and kissed my hands and the skirts of my gown .
