111279	111496	112079	112079	she	588	" Oh , Mrs. Bagot -- forgive _ you _ ! What a funny idea ! But , anyhow , you 've forgiven _ me _ , and that 's all I care for now . I was very fond of your son -- as fond as could be . I am now , but in quite a different sort of way , you know -- the sort of way _ you _ must be , I fancy ! There was never another like him that I ever met -- anywhere ! You _ must _ be so proud of him ; who would n't ? _ Nobody 's _ good enough for him . I would have been only too glad to be his servant , his humble servant ! I used to tell him so -- but he would n't hear of it -- he was much too kind ! He always thought of others before himself . And , oh ! how rich and famous he 's become ! I 've heard all about it , and it did me good . It does me more good to think of than anything else ; far more than if I were to be ever so rich and famous myself , I can tell you ! "
